=== 6. Cost estimate for this turn ===
Not pulled from OpenAI's billing dashboard (no billing API available in this
session) — computed from this run's actual measured audio/text lengths and
OpenAI's published per-unit rates:
  - whisper-1: 3.77s learner audio = 0.063 min * $0.006/min      = $0.00038
  - gpt-4o-mini: ~1000 input tok (est., system+context+utterance)
      * $0.15/1M + ~40 output tok * $0.60/1M                     = $0.00017
  - tts-1: 155 chars (tutor reply) * $0.000015/char               = $0.00233
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------
  Total, this turn: ~$0.0029 (the gpt-4o-mini input-token count is an
  estimate — the exact system-prompt length wasn't counted — everything
  else is measured directly from this run.)

=== 7. HTTPS / phone check ===
$ which tailscale caddy
/usr/local/bin/tailscale
(caddy not found)
$ tailscale status
Tailscale is stopped.
Starting/logging in the Tailscale daemon is a system-level network change
this lane did not make unattended (see docs/self-hosting.md). LAN reachability
itself was verified: the server bound 0.0.0.0 and printed
"Server listening at http://192.168.1.26:8792" alongside the loopback
listener. A real iPhone was not available in this environment to confirm
the HTTPS-for-microphone requirement directly; that gap is documented in
docs/self-hosting.md rather than asserted as verified.
